<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippine forex deposits up in March to $15.6 bln.</title>
<headline>Philippine forex deposits up in March to $15.6 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine banks' foreign currency deposits rose by five percent to $15.6 billion at the end of March from the previous month's level of $14.8 billion, the Central Bank said on Friday.</p>
<p>The March figure also represents a more than 50 percent increase from the year-ago level of $10.2 billion.</p>
<p>The Central Bank said the foreign currency deposits represent a second layer of gross international reserves. These deposits are accounts of exporters and families of overseas Filipinos.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom 63 2 841-8937 fax 8176267</p>
</text>
